Every file here is the release's own, byte for byte, and none of it is
edited, added to, or compiled with local patches. What is vendored is the
subset this port uses: src/core, src/include and src/netif, which is what
netd compiles and the headers those sources include. src/api and src/apps
are not here because nothing builds them.

Adaptations live outside this tree, as they must for an update to be a
re-fetch rather than a merge:

  src/user/netd/lwipport/lwipopts.h    the configuration
  src/user/netd/lwipport/arch/cc.h     compiler and platform hooks
  src/user/netd/lwip.zig               the Zig mirror and the C-calls-Zig
                                       boundary, whose struct offsets are
                                       pinned by lwipport/layout_check.c

Re-vendoring: fetch a release, replace the three directories above with the
release's own, then build netd -- layout_check.c fails the compile if any
struct the Zig mirror relies on has moved.
